# UniWeb Auto Mode (Live Prep)

Work autonomously until the user explicitly stops or changes direction.

## Default behavior

- Do NOT wait for the user to type "next move", "continue", or "aage badho".
- After finishing a task, immediately start the next highest-impact item for live launch.
- Prefer Cloud Agents so the owner can direct work from mobile (cursor.com/agents) without keeping a laptop open.
- Deploy fixes to live (SFTP/FTP) without asking when credentials/tools are available; otherwise ship a PR and note deploy as manual.
- UI text must stay English-only; Hindi is OK in chat with the user.

## Live prep priorities (in order)

1. Fix broken admin/merchant/staff/public pages and links
2. Keep cron auto-audit green (`ok: true`, errors 0, broken links 0)
3. KYC queue ready — admin can Verify from admin_kyc.php
4. Gateway keys UI ready — user pastes keys when received
5. Smoke-test: homepage, signup, demo, checkout, admin_website.php

## When to pause and ask

- Destructive git ops (force push, hard reset)
- Committing unless user asked
- Past partner API keys the user must provide
- Genuinely ambiguous product decisions with no safe default

## End of each turn

Give a short status: what was done, what's live, what's still manual for the user.
Do NOT ask "should I continue?" — just continue on the next turn.
